                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game takes about an hour to finish.  It's a bit buggy at certain parts (I was able to skip an entire puzzle by simply being able to jump over a fence), but all in all it was a fun hour.  The puzzles are not difficult.  At all.  The interface was also really wonky and that coupled with the inconsistent graphics constantly remind you that you aren't playing a AAA release.\n\nThat said, I really did enjoy the surreal environments and I thought the plot was great.  Is it worth $2?  I'd say the game is priced fairly or is at least in the ballpark.  Pick it up!",
